Title: First Day
Credit: original adaptation of a "new chief mistaken at the front desk" premise
Author: Claude (draft)
Format: 5 scenes x 16 s (each scene = 2 Flow generations of 8 s), English dialogue
Gate1: APPROVED by Owner 2026-11-01; amended SC03 (pieces laid on the counter, not dropped) per Owner "Lam buoc 5" 2026-11-01

INT. MAPLE FALLS POLICE STATION - LOBBY - MORNING

[[look: grey morning light through tall windows, worn tile floor, wooden front counter, a wall of old framed portraits]]

NORA HALE, a composed Black woman in her fifties, plain dark jacket, a folder under her arm, walks in and stops in the middle of the lobby. Behind the counter SGT. DOYLE, white, forties, uniform, sits with his boots up on the desk. He looks up, takes his boots down and stands.

DOYLE
(flat, not a question)
Help you, ma'am?

NORA
Good morning, Sergeant. I'm here to report for duty.

DOYLE laughs once, short and loud.

INT. MAPLE FALLS POLICE STATION - LOBBY - CONTINUOUS

NORA lays a police badge flat on the counter. DOYLE picks it up, turns it over once, then drops it into the metal trash can beside the desk. A loud clang.

DOYLE
Toy-store badge. Try again.

NORA does not move.

NORA
(even)
My name is Nora Hale. Today is my first day.

INT. MAPLE FALLS POLICE STATION - LOBBY - CONTINUOUS

NORA takes a folded letter from her folder and sets it on the counter. DOYLE unfolds it, glances at it, tears it in half, and in half again, and lays the pieces on the counter in front of her.

DOYLE
Fake papers too. You people will try anything.

[[beat: SILENCE]]
NORA gathers the pieces from the counter, folds them once and puts them in her jacket pocket. She straightens and looks at him. No anger. Patience.

INT. MAPLE FALLS POLICE STATION - LOBBY - CONTINUOUS

DOYLE unclips the handcuffs from his belt and holds them up between them.

DOYLE
(low)
Three seconds. Then you're under arrest.

NORA keeps her hands at her sides.

NORA
Call Lieutenant Commander Reed. Right now.

INT. MAPLE FALLS POLICE STATION - LOBBY - CONTINUOUS

LT. CMDR. REED, grey-haired, fifties, dress uniform, comes in from the hallway, sees NORA and stops at attention.

REED
Good morning, Chief Hale.

[[beat: REVEAL]]
DOYLE freezes. The handcuffs sink slowly in his hand.

NORA
(quiet)
Sergeant. Your badge. On the counter.

DOYLE slowly unpins his own badge and lays it on the counter.
